{{if and (ne .Language "go") (eq .ProjectType "worker")}}### 10. Jobs (Worker)
- One file per job: `src/jobs/<descriptiveName>Job.{{if .IsTypeScript}}ts{{else}}js{{end}}` exporting `JOB_NAME` and `run(log)`, registered explicitly in `src/schedulers/cron` (pattern + `lockTtlMs`). Run one now with `make run-job JOB=<name>`.
- Every scheduled run holds a Redis lock (`utils/lock`), so a job never runs twice at once across instances; `lockTtlMs` must exceed the worst-case duration. Keep runs **idempotent** (a retry or a manual run must be safe).
- **No database calls inside loops (N+1):** query in bulk, compute in memory, write in bulk (Drizzle `inArray`, multi-row `insert`).
- The API project owns the schema and migrations; `src/models/*` only mirrors the tables this worker uses. Never alter the schema from here.
- Log with the run logger (`log.info({ action, ... })`): counts and IDs, never PII or secrets.
{{end -}}
